To validate the model predictions, we performed photoconversion experiments in transgenic zebrafish embryos expressing the secreted Dendra2 in their brain ventricles. The approach is inspired by earlier work where a photoconvertible protein was injected into the ventricle [60]. By using a transgenic system where the protein is directly secreted into the CSF, we avoid detrimental effects of intraventricular injection on CSF properties. Our photoconversion protocol consisted of the acquisition of a baseline fluorescence intensity \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
